<task id="191" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>D7 Dataverse side: a flagged-external systemuser reaches no internal-only record, in Dataverse or the SPA (#2179 reopened)</title>
    <phase>Session 28: UAC (owner round 113, 2026-10-21)</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Security and tenant isolation; changes who can read rows directly in Dataverse; schema and share-job changes likely.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security design across Dataverse ownership, shares and the BFF; fails closed.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches the share/secure-root jobs and the access-permission columns that 188/189/190 also touch; runs after 188 merges.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>188 merged (BFF-side D7), 189 merged (stored = max(own, inherited))</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, security, access-control, tenant-isolation, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>design 1 day; build per design</estimated-effort>
    <origin>
      Owner round 113 (2026-10-21), verbatim in notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md "Round 113". Reverses round 111 item 5 (#2179 (c)) and the round-77 I-14 known limit. Expected to be the "real fix" for #1864 (ISS-010), which #2125 (ISS-014) and #2127 (ISS-016) wait on.
    </origin>
  </metadata>

  <goal>
A systemuser with sprk_isexternal = true must not read or change any internal-only record, whether directly in Dataverse (Web API, model-driven app) or through any BFF/SPA/Teams surface. Internal means internal to the customer. Internal-only records (owner-confirmed, round 113):
1. any record whose Access Permission is Restricted (Limited stays visible, round 111);
2. communications marked internal-only, and the documents attached to or derived from them (the 065 rule; sprk_relatedcommunication, sprk_parentdocument up to 3 hops);
3. all Procedure files (ebilling). Extracts of Procedures in rules or decision records that an external user may see are not affected.

Invoice and export files stay reachable by the related external user through the firm route (036 read set, I-14 veto, task 187 rule, file gate).

Open question carried in (ebilling 099 review, 2026-10-21): scorecard grades (`ScorecardCalculatorEndpoints`, /api/matters|projects/{id} grades) are derived from spend but sit outside /api/finance, so ebilling's step 0 does not refuse a flagged-external systemuser there; likewise `InsightsSearchEndpoint` and `WorkspaceAiEndpoints`. Decide in the design study whether they count as internal-only for a flagged-external systemuser.
  </goal>

  <design-checkpoint>
    BEFORE any schema, role or share change: the design study notes/2179-flagged-external-dataverse-design.md (inventory, Dataverse mechanisms, recommendation, owner questions) is reviewed by the main session and the owner's questions are answered. Cover Read and Write (no lowering Access Permission, unlinking from an internal-only communication or re-parenting), rows that become or stop being internal-only (revoke/regrant and timing), fail-closed, migration of existing shares, task 189 and the 065 rule, events and to-dos, and CLAUDE.md §11 answers.
  </design-checkpoint>

  <constraints>
    - ADR-002 (no plugins), ADR-028, ADR-052; one server-side owner per invariant (DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md).
    - Fail closed: an unreadable flag or internal-only state counts as external / internal-only.
    - No Entra, role, field-security, Key Vault or tenant-config write without explicit owner approval in-session.
    - The BFF-side D7 narrowing (task 188) stays; this task adds the Dataverse-side enforcement and closes the I-14 / #2179 known limit.
    - Logs carry ids and counts only.
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>A flagged-external systemuser cannot read a Restricted row, an internal-only communication, a document derived from one, or a Procedure file through the Dataverse Web API (live check on dev with a test flagged-external user).</criterion>
    <criterion>The same user cannot lower Access Permission, unlink a document from an internal-only communication or re-parent it out of a Restricted ancestor.</criterion>
    <criterion>An unflagged internal user with the same shares is unaffected (must-not-fire).</criterion>
    <criterion>A row that becomes internal-only is withdrawn within the stated window; one that stops being internal-only is regranted.</criterion>
    <criterion>#2125, #2127 and #1864 are closed by this work or explicitly re-scoped.</criterion>
    <criterion>I-14 and .claude/constraints/auth.md updated: the #2179 known limit is removed; Enforced by named.</criterion>
    <criterion>BFF build 0 errors; targeted tests green; full ArchTests green; publish-size delta measured; deployed to dev via R3 with a server-side live gate.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <outputs>
    - notes/2179-flagged-external-dataverse-design.md (design, checkpointed).
    - Code, scripts and tests on branch uac/191-flagged-external-dataverse (worktree C:/wt191), draft PR to master.
  </outputs>
</task>
